.\" Version and date on the .TH line are stamped by tools/stamp_version.py; do not edit by hand.
.TH DOCWRAITH 1 "2026-11-12" "docwraith 0.15.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
docwraith \- scan Office documents and PDFs for embedded AI instructions, hidden text and provenance markers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docwraith
.RI [ options ]
.IR path " [" path " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docwraith
examines Word (.docx), PowerPoint (.pptx), Excel (.xlsx), OpenDocument
(.odt/.ods/.odp) and PDF files for content that a human reader would not see
but an automated reader would, and for markers describing a file's origin and
integrity.
.PP
Each
.I path
is a file or a directory. Directories are scanned for recognized document
types; add
.B \-r
to recurse. A path may also be an archive (.zip, .tar, .tar.gz/.tgz, .rar),
whose document members are extracted to a temporary directory, scanned, and
then removed. Files are identified by content, not by extension, so a renamed
file is still classified correctly.
.PP
Findings fall into categories: prompt-injection instructions, hidden text,
Unicode smuggling, AI provenance tags, decoded watermarks, user search-term
matches, external references, review comments, and document-integrity
indicators. Each finding carries a severity of HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW or INFO.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Recurse into directories.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a JSON report on stdout instead of the text report. Mutually exclusive
with \fB\-\-sarif\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-sarif
Emit a SARIF 2.1.0 report on stdout, for code-scanning dashboards and CI.
Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-json\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-severity " LEVEL"
Hide findings below \fILEVEL\fR in the text report. One of INFO, LOW, MEDIUM,
HIGH. Default INFO.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " LEVEL"
Exit 1 if any finding is at or above \fILEVEL\fR. One of INFO, LOW, MEDIUM,
HIGH. Default MEDIUM.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Progress to stderr. Repeat for more detail: \fB\-v\fR prints one line per file,
\fB\-vv\fR adds per-page and per-part detail and lists each finding as it is
produced. Progress always goes to stderr so a \fB\-\-json\fR or \fB\-\-sarif\fR
report on stdout stays clean.
.TP
.BI \-\-find " STRING"
Report whether \fISTRING\fR appears anywhere in the document
(case-insensitive, matched against raw text, a normalized form, and the raw
bytes). Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-find\-regex " PATTERN"
As \fB\-\-find\fR, with a regular expression. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-find\-file " FILE"
Read search terms from \fIFILE\fR, one per line. Blank lines and lines starting
with \fB#\fR are ignored; a line starting with \fBre:\fR is a regular
expression. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-emails
Report every email address found, in body text, hidden text, metadata,
annotations or raw bytes.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write the report to \fIFILE\fR instead of stdout. The one-line summary still
prints to stdout and the exit code is unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-\-extract\-dir " DIR"
Parent directory for archive extraction, instead of the system temp location.
The temporary directory created under it is removed after scanning.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-members " N"
Maximum number of archive members to process before aborting the archive.
Default 10000.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-bytes " SIZE"
Total extracted-size cap for an archive. Accepts a K, M or G suffix. Default
300M.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-member\-bytes " SIZE"
Per-member extracted-size cap. Accepts a K, M or G suffix. Default 64M.
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " FILE"
Read a password for encrypted documents from \fIFILE\fR (first line). The
password is never passed on the command line.
.TP
.B \-\-password\-prompt
Prompt for a password on the terminal, without echoing it.
.TP
.B \-\-ocr
OCR embedded raster images and scan the recovered text. Needs the tesseract
engine and is slower, so it is off by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-isolate ", " \-\-no\-isolate
Scan each file in a child process bounded by memory, CPU and wall-clock limits,
so a crash, hang or allocation bomb in a parser is contained to one file.
Default on where the platform supports it (Linux and macOS).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Per-file wall-clock limit when isolating (default 120).
.TP
.BI \-\-mem\-limit " SIZE"
Per-file memory limit when isolating, with a K, M or G suffix (default 2G).
.TP
.BI \-\-cpu\-limit " SECONDS"
Per-file CPU-time limit when isolating (default 60).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No finding at or above the \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR level.
.TP
.B 1
At least one finding at or above the \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR level.
.TP
.B 2
Scan errors occurred and no finding reached the \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR level.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan one file:
.B docwraith resume.pdf
.TP
Scan a tree and fail a CI job only on HIGH findings:
.B docwraith \-\-fail\-on HIGH \-r ./inbox
.TP
Produce SARIF for a code-scanning dashboard:
.B docwraith \-\-sarif \-o results.sarif \-r ./inbox
.TP
Look inside an archive for a leaked address and log links:
.B docwraith \-\-emails bundle.zip
.TP
Hunt a watermark list and keep only notable findings:
.B docwraith \-\-find\-file terms.txt \-\-min\-severity LOW ./docs
.SH FILES
.TP
.I requirements.txt
Runtime dependencies: pypdf and (recommended) defusedxml.
.SH NOTES
docwraith parses attacker-controlled input and is hardened accordingly, but it is
not a sandbox. For bulk or hostile input, run it under \fBtimeout\fR(1) and a
memory \fBulimit\fR(1), ideally as an unprivileged user in a container. Install
\fBdefusedxml\fR for untrusted XML. A password for an encrypted document is
taken from \fB\-\-password\-file\fR, \fB\-\-password\-prompt\fR or the
\fBDOCWRAITH_PASSWORD\fR environment variable, never from the command line;
encrypted Office documents also need the \fBmsoffcrypto-tool\fR package.
\fB\-\-ocr\fR needs the \fBtesseract\fR engine and the \fBpytesseract\fR and
\fBPillow\fR packages. RAR support needs the \fBrarfile\fR package
and an external tool (\fBunrar\fR, \fBunar\fR, \fBbsdtar\fR or \fB7z\fR) on PATH.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation, the detection reference and the security model are in
\fIREADME.md\fR; the security-finding history is in
\fISECURITY_CHANGELOG.md\fR.
